-41- The Obligation of Employers to Women as referred to in (2) paragraph (1) shall be carried out by Employers while female workers are at the workplace and during working hours that have been determined.
Working hours as referred to in paragraph (2) apply (3) to Women who enter into employment agreements for a definite period as well as for an indefinite period. Fixed-term employment agreements entered into by (4) Employers and female workers must be made in writing and must use the Indonesian language and Latin script.
Fixed-term employment agreements made by (5) Employers and female workers may only be made for certain work which according to the type and nature or activity of the work will be completed within a certain time, namely as follows:
a. Work that is once completed or temporary in nature;
b. Work that is estimated to be completed within a not too long time;
c. Work that is seasonal in nature;
d. Work related to new products, new activities, or additional products that are still in trial or exploration; or
e. Work whose type and nature or activity is not permanent.
Fixed-term employment agreements made by (6) Employers and female workers cannot be entered into for work that is permanent in nature.
Fixed-term employment agreements that do not (7) meet the provisions as referred to in paragraph (5) ir and paragraph (6) shall by law become indefinite-term employment agreements.

