Second Part
Prevention of Acts of Violence Against Women Article 46 To anticipate and prevent acts of violence against Women from occurring, the Regional Government shall undertake the following efforts:
a.
b.
f.
provide various proper public facilities for Women in public spaces;
develop an integrated information system database on acts of violence against Women;
strengthen the competence of apparatus handling violence against Women;
create various modules and guidelines on the prevention and handling of acts of violence against Women;
conduct various training and guidance for social workers operating in organizations/institutions handling violence against Women;
invite the community to play an active role in recovery and reintegration;
strengthen the function of community organizations operating in the field of Women's empowerment; conduct various socialization regarding the prevention and anticipation of acts of violence against Women to various components of society in the Region; and optimize the role of religious institutions, customary institutions, culture, as well as exploration of local wisdom in order to prevent and minimize violence against Women occurring both at home or outside the home.

